sy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T17:59:39-07:00","id":183376,"title":"","content":"That's mostly due to the freelancers not being on the apocalypse team right? Stew is, either way, a very busy man.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T19:12:09-07:00","id":183430,"title":"","content":"There's freelancer crossover, but Stew has all the crossover.<br /> <br /> Besides, once the writers are done, Stew still has editing and developing duties. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T21:18:16-07:00","id":183495,"title":"","content":"Ain't no rest for the wolves.<br /> <br /> Powers That Be bless y'all for keeping that true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T00:06:19-07:00","id":183598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/182398-no-forsaken-friday-this-week-again?p=183352#post183352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The team is actually getting a lot done on <i>Idigam</i> right now. Redlines are back to writers, and they're working furiously on second drafts. So even if Stew doesn't have time to update this week, <i>Apocalypse</i> isn't slowing down <i>Forsaken</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, my <b>Apocalyspe</b> comment was a (bad) joke, but I'm happy to hear <b>Idigam</b> development goes with the plan. So we can assume that September date is possible to start of fund raising?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T00:11:23-07:00","id":183599,"title":"","content":"Unless OP has changed its mind, the Idigam Chronicle is not being Kickstarted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T00:24:23-07:00","id":183606,"title":"","content":"Wow, so what? It will be sell only on DriveThru? Will be a &quot;hardcover+PDF&quot; option available?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-29-2014, 03:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T01:23:34-07:00","id":183649,"title":"","content":"I believe it will be the same model as Blood &amp; Smoke - pdf first for readers to spot typos and problems, then offered in a range of print options, including Premium Colour Hardback. If OP stays true to its usual practice, early adopters of the pdf will get vouchers for the difference to purchase physical copies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T08:03:37-07:00","id":183793,"title":"","content":"Kinda wish we had a kickstarter, might be nice to get some stretch goals and make sure all the info we want is in it. Werewolves have a lot of enemies. Last time it took four years to cover the main ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T08:14:24-07:00","id":183806,"title":"","content":"While I would love to have a kickstarter, it seems unfair to the Blood and Smoke crowd to do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T08:24:16-07:00","id":183817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/182398-no-forsaken-friday-this-week-again?p=183806#post183806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I would love to have a kickstarter, it seems unfair to the Blood and Smoke crowd to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>As part of the Blood and Smoke crowd, I would have gladly backed them for more pages and to show my support in the project. While it's very comprehensive, many things could have been expanded upon for the better, and some things were left out entirely (Belial's Brood). And Vampire didn't have an alternate reality to deal with.<br /> <br /> But if someone were to complain about things being unfair, they might look at the difference between things like the 500+ page 20th anniversary editions, with cut content being spilled into other books available to backers, and compare that to the Chronicle books and notice an imbalance.<br /> <br /> Though to be entirely honest, I'm not sure Forsaken could manage to succeed on a Kickstarter at the same level other games have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T08:54:48-07:00","id":183848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/182398-no-forsaken-friday-this-week-again?p=183817#post183817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As part of the Blood and Smoke crowd, I would have gladly backed them for more pages and to show my support in the project. While it's very comprehensive, many things could have been expanded upon for the better, and some things were left out entirely (Belial's Brood). And Vampire didn't have an alternate reality to deal with.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll counter stating that you already have entire books worth setting material and adapting any of those it's incredibly easy.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T11:53:38-07:00","id":183922,"title":"","content":"Plus, there will be a NWOD Cross Settings book (<b><i>NWOD's Dark Eras</i></b>: Edit; I had a mind slip and called it Dark Ages. Doh.) set up for Kickstarter. And if anything, the developers/writers do listen to the Kickstarter comments. So if you wanted more Forsaken in different eras stuff there, it might happen.<br /> <br /> I'm also both an Apocalypse and Forsaken fan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","user":"Laughing Hyena","date":". 06-29-2014, 05:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T12:05:36-07:00","id":183945,"title":"","content":"Dark Eras. Just saying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T13:22:34-07:00","id":183993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/182398-no-forsaken-friday-this-week-again?p=183945#post183945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dark Eras. Just saying.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm middly interested in <b>Dark Eras</b> itself - enough to get PDF for <b>Mage</b> minisetting - but as I understand, the suporting of it on Kickstarter will add other setting to other gamelines, not <b>Forsaken</b>. As newly converted <b>Werewolf</b> fan, I would like to see as much possible changes to be in <b>Idigam </b><b>Chronicles</b>, and basic lore of 10 years of gameline combined in it, not like omitting Belial Brood in <b>Blood &amp; Smoke</b>. I know we have supplements, but without help of forumites, I wouldn't be able to find everything I need in it, or even basics outside of corebook - like half of stuff from <b>Lore of Forsaken</b>... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T13:38:32-07:00","id":184005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/182398-no-forsaken-friday-this-week-again?p=183993#post183993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm middly interested in <b>Dark Eras</b> itself - enough to get PDF for <b>Mage</b> minisetting - but as I understand, the suporting of it on Kickstarter will add other setting to other gamelines, not <b>Forsaken</b>. As newly converted <b>Werewolf</b> fan, I would like to see as much possible changes to be in <b>Idigam </b><b>Chronicles</b>, and basic lore of 10 years of gameline combined in it, not like omitting Belial Brood in <b>Blood &amp; Smoke</b>. I know we have supplements, but without help of forumites, I wouldn't be able to find everything I need in it, or even basics outside of corebook - like half of stuff from <b>Lore of Forsaken</b>... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> It's not like the supplemental books are going anywhere...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T14:16:17-07:00","id":184075,"title":"","content":"I was correcting Hyena, actually, but let's deal with this.<br /> <br /> 1) Supporting any Era on the Kickstarter results i more on that setting. It's not like it produces a new era for each game line. I don't think this was a serious concern, but still I figure it's worth addressing.<br /> <br /> 2) Let me clarify something: I own, like, three forsaken supplements-the Chronicler's Guide, Tribes of the Moon and Blood of the Wolf. I may have read other stuff over the years, but that's it.<br /> <br /> I have been able to do just fine and have lots of fun with the core book by itself.<br /> <br /> The supplements <i>really help</i> but they really aren't needed. Idigam bringing in that stuff is awesome as hell, but it's not a deal breaker, for me at least.<br /> <br /> 3).....did I have a third point. Oh well, it'll come to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T16:39:35-07:00","id":184194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/182398-no-forsaken-friday-this-week-again?p=184005#post184005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It's not like the supplemental books are going anywhere...</div> </div> </div> </div>Right? that's what I'm saying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T01:01:24-07:00","id":184649,"title":"","content":"Still nice to get as much as we can in the core though. Honestly I'm amazed at how small idigam is. I know new worlds rules are a lot more simplified then apocalypse but still... Course apocalypse does have 20+ years of lore...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T07:09:59-07:00","id":185493,"title":"","content":"Since there's been no Forsaken Friday I figure I'll mutter briefly about yesterday's playtest session I ran:<br /> - DaveB's Ithaeur ended up using smoke, poisoned meat and a butcher's knife while wearing a bone-and-antler mask in order to banish a Hunger spirit.<br /> - Much fun was had with Urshul handing out Tilts like candy.<br /> - We realised the Clash of Wills system REALLY needs to cover what happens when a werewolf's Facet clashes with a spirit's Influence.<br /> - On which note, last session saw the appearance of a door spirit. Those of my group who are veterans of my old Forsaken chronicles immediately knew they were in trouble.<br /> - The pack took on a Rank 1 Claimed, which was shit-hard. Seriously, those who decry the Storm Lords having Claimed as their chosen prey, Claimed are really fucking scary. OTOH, the Storm Lord Rahu got to cross off his 'Kill a Claimed' Aspiration!<br /> - DaveB's character comes from a family that has produced several Uratha. They have 'special' rooms down in the basement.<br /> - Some of the most absurd Perception rolls I have ever seen, meaning the level of information those werewolves' noses got was pretty in-depth. Mages might have all their magical woo to detect wibbly things, but a werewolf can really get to know you through entirely mundane senses :P<br /> - When the pack were making a getaway in a car, I decided that <i>obviously</i> a Hunger-Claimed's Hunger Influence extended to symbolic stuff like, say, the hunger of the car's engine gulping down petrol. The pack promptly had to bail and run off in Urhan after their car got through its entire tank of petrol in a couple of minutes.<br /> - We saw a Warding Facet that made it rather tricky for the pack to get to their target and kinda put paid to their stealth attempts, along with another Warding Facet that meant the enemy knew they'd breached the perimeter. We saw yet another Warding Facet used by a PC that was the cause of Player Versus Door Spirit's Influence (the player won, <i>just</i>.)<br /> - Wolf-Blooded - they're handy people to have around, especially when their reaction to their werewolf brother turning up with a tied-up guy in the car boot is to roll their eyes and lend a hand. Amusingly, it's the physically weakest of three brothers who Changed; the Ithaeur's siblings are sturdy fellows.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T08:03:24-07:00","id":185516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/182398-no-forsaken-friday-this-week-again?p=185493#post185493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since there's been no Forsaken Friday I figure I'll mutter briefly about yesterday's playtest session I ran:<br /> - DaveB's Ithaeur ended up using smoke, poisoned meat and a butcher's knife while wearing a bone-and-antler mask in order to banish a Hunger spirit.<br /> - Much fun was had with Urshul handing out Tilts like candy.<br /> - We realised the Clash of Wills system REALLY needs to cover what happens when a werewolf's Facet clashes with a spirit's Influence.<br /> - On which note, last session saw the appearance of a door spirit. Those of my group who are veterans of my old Forsaken chronicles immediately knew they were in trouble.<br /> - The pack took on a Rank 1 Claimed, which was shit-hard. Seriously, those who decry the Storm Lords having Claimed as their chosen prey, Claimed are really fucking scary. OTOH, the Storm Lord Rahu got to cross off his 'Kill a Claimed' Aspiration!<br /> - DaveB's character comes from a family that has produced several Uratha. They have 'special' rooms down in the basement.<br /> - Some of the most absurd Perception rolls I have ever seen, meaning the level of information those werewolves' noses got was pretty in-depth. Mages might have all their magical woo to detect wibbly things, but a werewolf can really get to know you through entirely mundane senses :P<br /> - When the pack were making a getaway in a car, I decided that <i>obviously</i> a Hunger-Claimed's Hunger Influence extended to symbolic stuff like, say, the hunger of the car's engine gulping down petrol. The pack promptly had to bail and run off in Urhan after their car got through its entire tank of petrol in a couple of minutes.<br /> - We saw a Warding Facet that made it rather tricky for the pack to get to their target and kinda put paid to their stealth attempts, along with another Warding Facet that meant the enemy knew they'd breached the perimeter. We saw yet another Warding Facet used by a PC that was the cause of Player Versus Door Spirit's Influence (the player won, <i>just</i>.)<br /> - Wolf-Blooded - they're handy people to have around, especially when their reaction to their werewolf brother turning up with a tied-up guy in the car boot is to roll their eyes and lend a hand. Amusingly, it's the physically weakest of three brothers who Changed; the Ithaeur's siblings are sturdy fellows.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't remember if Warding Facets have come up in the previews, or if that's something I don't remember from Core, but they sound annoying/awesome!<br /> <br /> You've touched on the most important aspect of Wolf-Blooded, and I'm looking forward to have a bunch of &quot;backup&quot; NPCs in case we do downtime sessions or B-team missions<br /> <br /> Finally, Tilts. I've been running Blood &amp; Smoke, so they haven't come up, but I'm excited to introduce them to my players.<br /> <br /> Even though this isn't Forsaken Friday content, it's just making me <i>even more excited</i> for Idigam Chronicles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T08:05:29-07:00","id":185518,"title":"","content":"Sounds fun. Definitely appears as if spirits will be a big threat on their own, along with the other spirit-antagonists. If a rank 1 claimed is as intimidating as you make out, particularly with the boost to werewolf healing, I'm definitely looking forward to the rules for them.<br /> <br /> I have to wonder, though, fluff-wise do they still act to sort of keep the Shadow and the real separate? Or, outside of when it affects them personally, do they keep their interest in that restrained until the Sacred Hunt?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T09:02:16-07:00","id":185577,"title":"","content":"So the 'Claimed' are people taken over by any sort of raging spirits, not just victims of weird niche parasite-things like Beshu or brain-spiders or rat-people? Huh. That's a lot cooler than I thought. And makes spirits a lot scarier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T09:14:01-07:00","id":185586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barbrarilen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/182398-no-forsaken-friday-this-week-again?p=185577#post185577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the 'Claimed' are people taken over by any sort of raging spirits, not just victims of weird niche parasite-things like Beshu or brain-spiders or rat-people? Huh. That's a lot cooler than I thought. And makes spirits a lot scarier.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, been the case since Forsaken was launched.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T09:14:34-07:00","id":185587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barbrarilen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/182398-no-forsaken-friday-this-week-again?p=185577#post185577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the 'Claimed' are people taken over by any sort of raging spirits, not just victims of weird niche parasite-things like Beshu or brain-spiders or rat-people? Huh. That's a lot cooler than I thought. And makes spirits a lot scarier.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what they've always been. You're thinking of the Hosts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T09:28:12-07:00","id":185599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barbrarilen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/182398-no-forsaken-friday-this-week-again?p=185577#post185577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the 'Claimed' are people taken over by any sort of raging spirits, not just victims of weird niche parasite-things like Beshu or brain-spiders or rat-people? Huh. That's a lot cooler than I thought. And makes spirits a lot scarier.</div> </div> </div> </div> The brain spider and rat people parasites (and by extension, the people controlled by them) are the Hosts. They're a very specific type of spirit-flesh amalgamation, distinct enough from regular, ephemeral spirits to be in a category of their own. They use different rules than normal spirits as well. Claimed, on the other hand are people whose bodies have been taken over completely by a spirit -any spirit- usually by repeated possession. Actually, Ghosts and Angels can cause the Claimed Condition now too, as long as they have the right manifestation(s) and meet the prerequisite Conditions.","signature":"<